{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"action\":\"request-ruling\",\"rationale\":\"The latest verifier resolved the prior production refresh-stub blocker but found a new blocking ambiguity: project-shell UI offers refresh for stale/not_hydrated project-scoped sources while the backend now rejects project-scoped refresh unless exactly one current process owns the working copy. The story-local requirements require refresh paths on project and process source surfaces, but do not define the target semantics for project-scoped refresh when zero or multiple processes reference the attachment. This is a product/scope decision, not a verifier or implementor guess.\",\"inputs\":{\"decisionType\":\"project-scoped-refresh-semantics\",\"question\":\"For project-scoped source attachments shown in the project shell, what should refresh do when the attachment is stale or not_hydrated but there is no single unambiguous current process working-copy target?\",\"defaultRecommendation\":\"Hide or disable the project-shell refresh control unless the backend can identify exactly one current process working-copy target; keep refresh enabled for process-scoped rows and for project-scoped rows with one unambiguous owning process. This avoids falsely promising recovery and aligns with AC-3.2 until a later story defines cross-process/project-level hydration semantics.\",\"evidence\":[\"Verifier finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity is blocking and affects AC-3.2, AC-3.3, TC-3.2a, TC-3.2c, and TC-3.3a.\",\"Client project source section renders refresh controls for any stale or not_hydrated source regardless of scope.\",\"RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor returns SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source.\",\"All gates passed, but verifier outcome is needs-human-ruling because story-local requirements do not define project-scoped refresh target selection.\"],\"allowedResponses\":[\"Disable/hide project-shell refresh unless a single current process target exists; continue implementation to make UI truthful.\",\"Define project-scoped refresh to automatically select or create a runtime target; continue implementation with that behavior.\",\"Treat project-scoped refresh ambiguity as out of scope for Story 3 and allow current backend rejection despite the visible UI control.\",\"Block Story 3 until a separate design update defines project-scoped refresh semantics.\"]}}"}}
